<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of La Forbie</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1244</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Battle of Hiribya</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of La Forbie was fought on 17–18 October 1244 near Gaza between the army of the Ayyubid sultan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, as-Salih Ayyub, with Khwarazmian allies under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baybars">Baybars</a>, and an alliance of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusader-states">Crusader states</a> with the Ayyubid rulers of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/homs">Homs</a>. The Egyptian victory destroyed the last large Crusader field army and confirmed Muslim control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>, which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khwarazmians">Khwarazmians</a> had sacked that summer.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-la-forbie.jpg" alt="Battle of La Forbie" width="320" height="171" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Matthew Paris · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:La_Forbie.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
